WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.020
A staged pipeline uses inexpensive analysis to decide when deeper analysis is worth the cost.

2
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.120
Motion or scene-change logic can create a candidate window.

3
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:13.740
Object detection can identify configured categories and zones.

4
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.920
Tracking or event rules group repeated detections across frames.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:23.960
Selected clips may then reach scene-description or vision-language models for richer summaries.

6
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:32.300
This later stage should receive enough preceding and following context to avoid describing an isolated frame as a complete event.

7
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:37.060
Confidence scoring and thresholds control how candidates advance.

8
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:42.040
A low threshold improves sensitivity while increasing compute and false positives.

9
00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:49.420
Separate thresholds can be used for storage, routine review, and urgent alerting rather than forcing one decision point.

10
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:54.980
Multiple stages can reduce cost and noise, but each stage can also discard a real event.

11
00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:59.960
Measure false positives and false negatives end to end.

12
00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:04.220
A strong final model cannot recover frames that an earlier trigger never selected.

13
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:09.620
Version models, prompts, rules, zones, and thresholds.

14
00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:14.040
Record the versions with each event so behavior can be explained after updates.

15
00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:20.780
Evaluate representative footage across cameras, lighting, weather, and common harmless activity.

16
00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:25.940
The pipeline should communicate uncertainty and preserve human review.

17
00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:29.800
Model output is assistance, not proof of identity or intent.

18
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:38.300
Design fallback behavior when a model is unavailable, queues are delayed, or compute is saturated, and make degraded analysis visible to operators.
